<Base
  title="About Calquna"
  description="Calquna is a small set of free calculators that show their working. Who runs it, and how the pages are checked."
>
  <h1>About Calquna</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Calquna is a one-person project: a set of free calculators built carefully, one at a time,
    instead of a few hundred built carelessly at once.
  </p>
  <p>
    The idea is simple. Most calculator sites give you a number and ask you to trust it. Every
    page here prints the formula it used, one example worked through by hand, and the date the
    page was last checked. If you can follow the working, you do not have to trust anyone.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is run by Ahmad Ameen, a software developer in Pakistan who has built websites
    and tools for clients since 2015. Calquna is written in English, Spanish and French. The
    Spanish and French pages are translated and then read through by a person before they go
    up, because a calculator that reads badly in your language is not much use to you.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is paid for by advertising, which is why it is free and why there is no account to
    make. Nothing you type into a calculator is sent to a server, stored, or sold. There is
    nothing to sell: the sums happen in your browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    Found a wrong answer, or a sentence that makes no sense? That is the most useful email
    this site can get. Use the contact page.
  </p>
  <p class="meta">Page last checked 13 November 2026.</p>
</Base>
